WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.940
- Sometimes I love Bad Legal Takes,

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.790
especially when they come
from add Bad Legal Takes.

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.930
And this one I think came up
in the context of Section 230.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.460
Someone says, "Google is
a monopoly and therefore,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.760
I guess, not a private company".

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.980
To which Ari Cohn,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.517
who is generally an excellent
legal commentator chimes in,

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:16.770
"Even if it was monopoly(and it's not),

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.640
that...doesn't make it
not a private company."

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.217
To which the commentator
helpfully responds,

00:00:21.217 --> 00:00:22.750
"Before you try and be a smart,

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.990
Look up some basic definitions.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.970
Let me start you off with
a public company is one

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.740
that is traded publicly
in the open market.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.970
And Google? Well look!

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:29.820
The company went public

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.330
via initial public offering in 2004".

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.410
Public. No!

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.410
Oh, no! So this is a
horrible, horrible legal take

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.840
because admittedly, there
are two different definitions

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.673
of a public company.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.310
One is a public company that's
owned by the government.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.680
The First Amendment
applies to the government.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:45.513
And if you are the government,

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:46.850
then the First Amendment applies.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.930
Then second, a
publicly-traded company is one

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.230
that just has stock that you
can purchase on an exchange.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.350
It doesn't mean that they are owned

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.760
or operated by the government.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.880
And if you are a
publicly-traded private company,

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.980
the First Amendment does not apply to you.

